<%#
  contract-detail.ejs — Screen 7, Contract detail with print and download
  (AS-47).

  Built to docs/design/wireframes/screen-7-contract-detail.html and its ledger,
  02-states-ledger.md §7. Every element the wireframe marks `data-wf-note` is
  wireframe annotation and is deliberately NOT built (01-screens.md §6).

  PRESENTATION ONLY. Every decision was made in
  lib/screens/contract-detail-view.js; this file branches on precomputed
  booleans (isDownload, isDefault, isNotFound, isSystem) and reads properties.
  It does NOT branch on state ids. Four properties hold over it, each a concept
  row in test/dependency-policy.test.js rather than a convention (README.md
  § The view layer):

    P1  no raw-output tag anywhere — EXCEPT ONE LINE. THIS FILE CARRIES THE ONE
        SANCTIONED RAW-OUTPUT LINE IN THIS APP: the line that emits
        renderedHtml inside the document region. It is pinned by the
        RAW_OUTPUT_SANCTIONED allowlist to its exact text as the WHOLE line,
        count 1 — a second expression on that line un-sanctions it, and a
        second such line anywhere is a finding. The value is the stored
        document produced by lib/contracts/render.js: every text node in it
        went through that file's one escaper and no data reaches an attribute
        position there, so it is safe in element content — the only position
        this line puts it in. Escaping it AGAIN would render the document's own
        tags as text.
    P2  no interpolation in an href/src/action/formaction/style attribute, no
        event-handler attribute, no script or style element
    P3  every attribute value carrying data is DOUBLE-quoted
    P4  within any start tag, every output tag sits inside an attribute value

  NOTE FOR ANYONE EDITING THIS COMMENT: do not spell the raw-output tag or a
  closing EJS tag inside it. The dependency-policy scanner strips an EJS
  comment up to its FIRST closing tag, so a spelled-out example would both
  truncate the strip and plant an unsanctioned hit.

  THE DOWNLOAD VARIANT (plan §3.4). When isDownload is true the body is the
  document region alone — no header, no nav, no heading, no actions — and the
  route answers it as an attachment. The head is identical in both variants,
  so the shared "every registered template links both stylesheets" check stays
  literally true and this template has one head; opened from disk the two
  root-relative links resolve against file:// and reach nothing, so the
  downloaded file phones nobody and is unstyled by construction.

  NO PRINT CONTROL (plan §3.5). window.print() needs a script and this app has
  none (P2c). One sentence points at the browser's Print command, and the
  @media print block in public/app.css hides the chrome, the heading and the
  actions so the sheet carries the document alone.

  THE NAV (01-screens.md §3: screens 3-7 carry it). Constant markup:
  Dashboard (`/`, AS-48's screen 3 — its anchor landed with it, first in the
  nav, and NOTFOUND's "Back to Dashboard" line (the wireframe's) landed in the
  same commit, a constant href to a route that now exists), New invoice
  (/invoices/new, AS-46's screen), New contract (/contracts/new, screen 6 —
  landed by AS-127 in the same change as the route it points at, because a
  nav link to a route that does not exist is a shipped path ending on a 404)
  and Sign out.
-%>
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-state="<%= state %>">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Invoicing — <%= title %></title>
    <%# The vendored single source of visual truth, served byte-identical by
        routes/assets.js. Never a local copy. %>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/tokens.css" />
    <%# App-owned styles, served from public/ by express.static. %>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/app.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <% if (!isDownload) { %>
      <header class="site-header">
        <div class="container site-header__inner">
          <span class="app-label">Invoicing</span>
        </div>
        <div class="container">
          <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Primary">
            <a class="site-nav__link" href="/">Dashboard</a>
            <a class="site-nav__link" href="/invoices/new">New invoice</a>
            <a class="site-nav__link" href="/contracts/new">New contract</a>
            <form class="site-nav__signout" method="post" action="/signout">
              <button type="submit" class="btn-link">Sign out</button>
            </form>
          </nav>
        </div>
      </header>
    <% } %>

    <main class="container">
      <% if (!isDownload) { %>
        <h1 class="page-title"><%= title %></h1>
      <% } %>

      <% if (isNotFound) { %>
        <div class="banner banner-error">
          <p><%= banner %></p>
        </div>
        <p><a href="/">Back to Dashboard</a></p>
      <% } %>

      <% if (isSystem) { %>
        <div class="banner banner-error">
          <p><%= banner %></p>
        </div>
        <%# Retry is a GET of the page's own URL: no action attribute, so no
            id sits in a URL position (P2a). The wireframe's type="button" is a
            script affordance and is not built. %>
        <form method="get">
          <div class="form-actions">
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary"><%= retryLabel %></button>
          </div>
        </form>
      <% } %>

      <% if (isDefault) { %>
        <% if (!isDownload) { %>
          <div class="doc-actions">
            <p class="page-meta"><%= printHelp %></p>
            <%# Download submits ONE CONSTANT to the page's own URL (no action
                attribute): a presence flag the route reads as a boolean.
                Nothing user-supplied travels in a URL. %>
            <form method="get">
              <input type="hidden" name="download" value="1" />
              <button type="submit" class="btn btn-secondary"><%= downloadLabel %></button>
            </form>
          </div>
        <% } %>
        <div class="doc-region">
<%- renderedHtml %>
        </div>
      <% } %>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
